{"acceptance_length": 6.423076923076923, "acceptance_lengths": [5, 5, 11, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 11, 2, 3, 3, 4, 6, 16, 5, 16, 3, 1, 3, 2, 7, 3, 2, 7, 4, 4, 6, 4, 3, 7, 2, 16, 5, 6, 4, 1, 2, 2, 13, 15, 9, 6, 11, 16, 4, 16, 2, 13, 16, 16, 8], "accepted_draft_lengths": [4, 4, 10, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 10, 1, 2, 2, 3, 5, 15, 4, 15, 2, 0, 2, 1, 6, 2, 1, 6, 3, 3, 5, 3, 2, 6, 1, 15, 4, 5, 3, 0, 1, 1, 12, 14, 8, 5, 10, 15, 3, 15, 1, 12, 15, 15, 7], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23388434432, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23388417024, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "Let's break down the problem step by step to find the total cost of the trip.\n\n---\n\n### **1. Plane Tickets:**\n\n- Each ticket costs **$5000**.\n- There are 2 people (Tom and his wife), so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Cost of plane tickets} = 2 \\times 5000 = \\boxed{10000}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **2. Hotel Cost:**\n\n- **Normal price** of the hotel per day = **$1500**\n- The weekend is busy, so the hotel is **20% more expensive**.\n- First, calculate the **20% increase**:\n\n$$\n20\\% \\text{ of } 1500 = 0.20 \\times 1500 = 300\n$$\n\n- So, the **cost per day during the busy weekend** is:\n\n$$\n1500 + 300 = \\boxed{1800}\n$$\n\n- They are there for **3 days**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Hotel cost} = 3 \\times 1800 = \\boxed{5400}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **3. Total Cost of the Trip:**\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = \\text{Plane tickets} + \\text{Hotel cost} = 10000 + 5400 = \\boxed{15400}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{15400}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 1.895212575327605, "draft_calls": 52, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 97, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "a53b21494b39f7139d3a04b206a5698dbf22fbd0fa7192f8f9cc577bcf4a59e9", "method": "relay_two", "output_hash": "a893928a8a4b616d714f6a5e24dd1e052482274d3c32f33f6f023cbc96b3dd57", "output_tokens": 335, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23520338432, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23792189440, "problem_id": "gsm8k/051ae2b51a5de494", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 325.91078424453735